    "number": 313,
    "title": "fix: revert half-implemented nested_storage_collections lint that breaks main",
    "body": "## Why\n\n`main` is failing the required `lint` check and **no PR in this repo can merge** until this lands. Found while triaging the open PR backlog.\n\n## Root cause\n\n0a3295d (`feat: implement nested_storage_collections lint (#267)`) does not actually implement a lint. Its commit message claims it adds a `NestedStorageCollections` late lint pass, but the merged tree contains **no `declare_lint!`, no `impl LateLintPass`, and no registration** — the squash appears to have dropped them.\n\nWhat actually landed:\n\n- `SOROBAN_NESTABLE_COLLECTION_TYPES`, `is_soroban_collection()` and `has_nested_soroban_collection()` — none of which are reachable from any lint pass.\n- `docs/lints/nested_storage_collections.md` plus README/rationale entries **documenting a lint that does not exist**.\n\nBecause the helpers are unreachable, `-D warnings` fails:\n\n```\nerror: constant `SOROBAN_NESTABLE_COLLECTION_TYPES` is never used\n  --> soroban_cost_lints/src/lib.rs:161:7\n  = note: `-D dead-code` implied by `-D warnings`\n```\n\n## This PR\n\nStraight revert of 0a3295d. `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` both pass locally afterwards.\n\nReverting rather than completing the wiring is deliberate: the lint's detection semantics (which generic positions to flag, how to handle the `#[allow]` suppression case, what the UI fixtures should assert) are a maintainer call, and the shipped docs shouldn't describe behaviour the binary doesn't have.\n\n## Follow-up\n\nThe underlying issue should be reopened and reimplemented with the lint actually declared, registered, and covered by UI fixtures. The reverted `docs/lints/nested_storage_collections.md` is a reasonable starting spec.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TBuZPYykPjk7Tko2sJ6KHN",
